From d5763302b6ef12b3c5d314ed401f77a306ec2aa0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PabloBenario <pablo.benario@ug.uchile.cl>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 18:35:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Recognize failwith "TODO:..." natively as Incomplete

Add a when-guarded arm to protect_test so Failure messages beginning with
"TODO:" route to `Incomplete instead of `Exn. Mirrors the prefix matcher
used by QCheck2's todo_reason helper in qcheck-inc. Enables plain alcotest
tests (no QCheck in the loop) to mark themselves [INCOMPLETE] via
failwith "TODO:..." alone.

Alcotest.incomplete "reason" continues to work unchanged via the existing
Incomplete-exception arm one line above.
---
 src/alcotest-engine/core.ml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/alcotest-engine/core.ml b/src/alcotest-engine/core.ml
index e4ac508..a1e1c6a 100644
--- a/src/alcotest-engine/core.ml
+++ b/src/alcotest-engine/core.ml
@@ -191,6 +191,7 @@ module Make (P : Platform.MAKER) (M : Monad.S) = struct
              `Error (path, err)
          | Skip -> `Skip
          | Incomplete msg -> `Incomplete msg
+         | Failure s when String.is_prefix ~affix:"TODO:" s -> `Incomplete s
          | Failure s -> exn path "failure" Fmt.(const string s)
          | Invalid_argument s -> exn path "invalid" Fmt.(const string s)
          | e -> exn path "exception" Fmt.(const exn e))
-- 
