From 1253bef3767d3b4a14714bece49c8b05d8be8d50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PabloBenario <pablo.benario@ug.uchile.cl>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 19:20:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Drop redundant Incomplete exception and helper
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The failwith "TODO:..." when-guard in protect_test subsumes everything
the typed Incomplete exception + Alcotest.incomplete helper did. Both
paths produced the same `Incomplete variant; keeping both meant an
unnecessary second entry to the same outcome.

This commit removes:
  - exception Incomplete of string (core.ml, core_intf.ml, V1 re-export)
  - val Alcotest.incomplete : string -> 'a (test.ml, test.mli)
  - the `Incomplete msg -> ` arm in protect_test

What stays (the actual feature):
  - `Incomplete of string variant in Run_result.t
  - is_failure=false, has_run=true
  - [INCOMPLETE] tag rendering (yellow, compact char 'I')
  - `Failure s when String.is_prefix ~affix:"TODO:" s` arm in protect_test

Callers wanting to mark a test incomplete now use failwith "TODO:reason"
directly — same convention as every other consumer of the TODO prefix.
Net patch footprint drops from ~26 to ~12 lines across 6 files.
---
