From b33249b6559793a00b383504e71a9635a467c51d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PabloBenario <pablo.benario@ug.uchile.cl>
Date: Thu, 23 Apr 2026 12:44:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Add e2e regression test for the failwith "TODO:..."
 native path

Mirrors skip_in_test.ml one-for-one. A minimal runner with two cases:
one that returns unit normally (tagged [OK]) and one whose body raises
Failure via `failwith "TODO: not yet implemented"` (tagged [INCOMPLETE]
by the when-guard in protect_test). Expected output shows green + yellow
only, "Test Successful", exit 0.

If a future refactor ever removed the when-guard from protect_test, the
TODO case would be tagged [FAIL] instead, the summary would say "1
failure!", and the diff against incomplete_in_test.expected would fire.
This is the self-contained regression guard for the new arm.

Files touched:
  - test/e2e/alcotest/passing/incomplete_in_test.ml (new)
  - test/e2e/alcotest/passing/incomplete_in_test.expected (new)
  - test/e2e/alcotest/passing/dune.inc (auto-regenerated by
    gen_dune_rules.exe, adding the two rule stanzas for the new test)
